title: "AI-Assisted Social Science Research: Methods, Governance and Reason Provenance"
authors:
  - family-names: "Rudkin"
    given-names: "Simon"
    affiliation: "Department of Social Statistics, University of Manchester"
version: "0.3.12"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository: "https://github.com/srudkin12/GenerativeAI"
url: "https://srudkin12.github.io/GenerativeAI/"
abstract: >-
  A practical social-science resource on generative-AI-assisted research. The
  resource connects proposal generation, verification, adversarial challenge,
  claim authorisation, reason provenance and manuscript governance through
  transferable methods, worked research episodes and reusable tools.
keywords:
  - "social science"
  - "generative AI"
  - "research methods"
  - "reason provenance"
  - "manuscript governance"
  - "claim preservation"
  - "research transparency"
  - "AI-assisted research"
